<title>CHILE: Chilgener orders power line for $50 mln.</title>
<headline>Chilgener orders power line for $50 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilgener SA, Chile's second largest electric generator, said Wednesday it awarded Spain's Grupo Abengoa Argentine unit Teyma Abengoa a $50 million contract for power line between Chile and Argentina.</p>
<p>The contract entails constructing in Argentina's northern Salta province a 263 km line as part of the Inter Andes project.</p>
<p>Works will start in May and the line will be operative in December 1998, Chilgener general manager Juan Antonio Guzman said.</p>
<p>((--Santiago Newsroom, 562-672 8800))</p>
</text>
